    "result_text": "The build passes green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), as a **derived** read-only field \u2014 the right fit since both inputs (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`) are already persisted on the `Owner`, so no redundant column is needed. This mirrors the existing `displayName`/`initials` derivation rather than the persisted-field pattern (`customerCode`, `namesakeCount`).\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto` plus a small single-responsibility `membershipNumber(Owner)` default method that formats `customerCode` + `-M` + the zero-padded last two digits of the registration year (`getYear() % 100`, `%02d`). It null-guards when either input is absent.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
